Workstream ID: focus-room
Title: Fullscreen focus room and persistent distraction reports
Status: DONE
Milestone: Optional focused sessions with portable self-reported activity
Dependencies: career-graph
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/5
Purpose: Record the optional tab-local focus timer and persistent distraction
  events, preserving the distinction between time spent, self-report and mastery.

Tasks:
  [x] Share one tab-local timer controller across compact/fullscreen views.
  [x] Persist distraction presses immediately through guarded workspace updates.
  [x] Retain reports after timer reset/reload and include them in normal backups.
  [x] Snapshot the actual graph with independent, reduced-motion-aware ambience.
  [x] Isolate practice records and reject stale/same-ID replaced session writes.

Acceptance criteria:
  Closing/resetting the timer does not erase existing reports.
  Imported records do not become an inferred running countdown.
  Timer pause does not silently disable independently selected graph ambience.
  Reports and elapsed time never grant checkpoint credit.
  Practice cannot change the real timer or saved personal sessions.

Completion evidence:
  Retrospective authored: 2026-11-06.
  Public revisions: 9b22994, fdfb477, 558e4bd, 581cbe8, 091d751 and 2c3e4e7.
  Current source contract: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md; src/domain/focusSession.ts;
    src/focus; focus-room explanation in docs/GUIDE.md.
  Historical gate:
    https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/actions/runs/41529974393 at 9b2903b.
  Human acceptance: actual focus habits or user session outcomes not inspected.
  Publication: implementation already public; no focus feature edits here.
  Limitations: no live user session, foreground window or private browser accessed.

Completion log:
